batch_outputs:  [["731 × 962 = 703, 1462 + 43860 + 657900 = 703, 1462 + 43860 = 45322; 45322 + 657900 = 703,222.\n\nWait, that doesn't seem right. Let me check my calculations again.\n\nFirst, 731 × 2 = 1,462.\n\nNext, 731 × 60 = 43,860.\n\nThen, 731 × 900 = 657,900.\n\nNow, adding them up: 1,462 + 43,860 = 45,322.\n\nThen, 45,322 + 657,900 = 703,222.\n\nHmm, that still doesn't seem correct. Let me try another approach.\n\nAlternatively, I can use the standard multiplication method:\n\n```\n    731\n  × 962\n  -------\n    1462   (731 × 2)\n   43860   (731 × 60)\n +657900   (731 × 900)\n ---------\n  703,222\n```\n\nWait, that's the same result as before. Maybe I made a mistake in the initial breakdown. Let me verify using another method, such as breaking down 962 into 900 + 60 + 2.\n\nCalculating each part:\n\n731 × 900 = 657,900\n\n731 × 60 = 43,860\n\n731 × 2 = 1,462\n\nAdding them together: 657,900 + 43,860 = 701,760\n\n701,760 + 1,462 = 703,222\n\nIt seems consistent. Therefore, the correct product is 703,222.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 731 and 962 is \\boxed{703222}.\n</think>\n\nLet's think step by step.\n\n1. Multiply 731 by 2 (the ones place digit of 962):\n   \\[\n   731 \\times 2 = 1462\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 731 by 60 (the tens place digit of 962):\n   \\[\n   731 \\times 60 = 43860\n   \\]\n\n3. Multiply 731 by 900 (the hundreds place digit of 962):\n   \\[\n   731 \\times 900 = 657900\n   \\]\n\nNow, sum all the step results:\n\\[\n1462 + 43860 + 657900 = 703222\n\\]\n\nSo, the final computed product is \\(\\boxed{703222}\\).", '']]
