batch_outputs:  [["609, 917 multiplied by 664 equals 609, 917 × 664 = 609.\n\nWait, that doesn't seem right. Let me check my calculations again.\n\nFirst, multiply 917 by 4: 917 × 4 = 3,668.\n\nNext, multiply 917 by 60: 917 × 60 = 55,020.\n\nThen, multiply 917 by 600: 917 × 600 = 550,200.\n\nNow, add all these results together: 3,668 + 55,020 + 550,200 = 608,888.\n\nSo, the correct product of 917 and 664 is 608,888.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 917 and 664?\n\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. 664 has three digits, so we can break it down into three steps.\n\n1. Multiply 917 by 4 (the ones place digit of 664):\n   \\[\n   917 \\times 4 = 3,\\!668\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 917 by 60 (the tens place digit of 664):\n   \\[\n   917 \\times 60 = 55,\\!020\n   \\]\n\n3. Multiply 917 by 600 (the hundreds place digit of 664):\n   \\[\n   917 \\times 600 = 550,\\!200\n   \\]\n\nNow, sum all the step results:\n\\[\n3,\\!668 + 55,\\!020 + 550,\\!200 = 608,\\!888\n\\]\n\n# Answer:\nThe product of 917 and 664 is \\(\\boxed{608,\\!888}\\).", '']]
