      "text": "746 \u00d7 536 = 400, 296.\n\nWait, that doesn't seem right. Let me check my calculations again.\n\nFirst, multiply 746 by 6:\n746 \u00d7 6 = 4,476\n\nNext, multiply 746 by 30:\n746 \u00d7 30 = 22,380\n\nThen, multiply 746 by 500:\n746 \u00d7 500 = 373,000\n\nNow, add all these results together:\n4,476 + 22,380 = 26,856\n26,856 + 373,000 = 400, 296\n\nHmm, that still doesn't look correct. Let me try adding them again carefully.\n\n4,476 + 22,380 = 26,856\n26,856 + 373,000 = 400, 296\n\nWait, 26,856 + 373,000 should be 400, 296? That doesn't add up. Let me do the addition step by step.\n\n26,856 + 373,000:\n26,856 + 300,000 = 326,856\n326,856 + 73,000 = 400, 296\n\nYes, that's correct. So, the final product is 400,296.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 746 and 536 is \\boxed{400296}.\n</think>\n\nLet's think step by step.\n\n1. Multiply 746 by 6 (the ones place digit of 536):\n   \\[\n   746 \\times 6 = 4476\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 746 by 30 (the tens place digit of 536):\n   \\[\n   746 \\times 30 = 22380\n   \\]\n\n3. Multiply 746 by 500 (the hundreds place digit of 536):\n   \\[\n   746 \\times 500 = 373000\n   \\]\n\nNow, sum all the step results:\n\\[\n4476 + 22380 + 373000 = 400296\n\\]\n\nSo, the final computed product is \\boxed{400296}.",
