batch_outputs:  [["192, 744 multiplied by 259 equals 192, 744 × 259 = 192.\n\nWait, that doesn't seem right. Let me check my calculations again.\n\nFirst, I'll multiply 744 by 9:\n744 × 9 = 6,696\n\nNext, I'll multiply 744 by 50:\n744 × 50 = 37,200\n\nThen, I'll multiply 744 by 200:\n744 × 200 = 148,800\n\nNow, I'll add all these results together:\n6,696 + 37,200 = 43,896\n43,896 + 148,800 = 192,696\n\nSo, the correct product of 744 and 259 is 192,696.\n\n**Answer:** The product of 744 and 259 is 192,696.\n\n# Final Answer\nThe product of 744 and 259 is \\boxed{192696}.\n</think>\n\nLet's think step by step.\n\n1. Multiply 744 by 9 (the ones place digit of 259):\n   \\[\n   744 \\times 9 = 6696\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 744 by 50 (the tens place digit of 259):\n   \\[\n   744 \\times 50 = 37200\n   \\]\n\n3. Multiply 744 by 200 (the hundreds place digit of 259):\n   \\[\n   744 \\times 200 = 148800\n   \\]\n\nNow, sum all the step results:\n\\[\n6696 + 37200 + 148800 = 192696\n\\]\n\nSo, the final computed product is \\boxed{192696}.", '']]
